    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). There's only the one test class in this repo, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `email` field to owners that is validated and stored/returned lower-cased.\n\n**Behaviour** (per spec):\n- Absent \u2192 accepted.\n- Present and syntactically valid \u2192 stored and returned lower-cased.\n- Present but invalid \u2192 rejected with `400`.\n\n**Changes (kept structurally cheap):**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` property (`type: string, format: email`) to `OwnerFields`. Because it's `format: email` with bean-validation on, the generated DTO carries `@Email`, so an invalid address yields a `400` through the existing validation-error handling \u2014 no new controller/exception code.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` column field plus a small getter/setter pair (each CC 1). MapStruct maps it automatically by name, so no mapper change.\n3. **`OwnerFieldsValidator.java`** \u2014 added 3 lines to lower-case the email when present, reusing the existing DTO-mutation path already used for telephone. This class has near-zero surrounding complexity, so the edit cost stays low.\n4. **DB schema/data** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added a nullable `email` column and fixed the positional seed `INSERT`s (hsqldb/mysql) so the count matches; h2/postgres already use explicit column lists.\n\nI avoided touching any of the large controller/service classes \u2014 the logic lives in the small validator and the schema-driven DTO, so no high-`WMC_other` method was modified.",
